  "description": "<p class=\"p1\" style=\"margin-bottom: 0px; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 13px; line-height: normal; font-family: \"Helvetica Neue\";\">We designed and patented the first and only sling with a hub for interchangeable attachments. When you connect an attachment into the sling, we call it a LifeHandle sling system.</p><p class=\"p2\" style=\"margin-bottom: 0px; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 13px; line-height: normal; font-family: \"Helvetica Neue\"; min-height: 15px;\"><br></p><p class=\"p1\" style=\"margin-bottom: 0px; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 13px; line-height: normal; font-family: \"Helvetica Neue\";\">The first system we made is a hands-free dog leash, which you get by connecting our custom leash into the sling. It’s the only hands-free leash on the market that actually works for long term, day-to-day use, and was designed to help with a dog’s pull force on our bodies. </p><p class=\"p2\" style=\"margin-bottom: 0px; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 13px; line-height: normal; font-family: \"Helvetica Neue\"; min-height: 15px;\"><br></p><p class=\"p1\" style=\"margin-bottom: 0px; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-stretch: normal; font-size: 13px; line-height: normal; font-family: \"Helvetica Neue\";\">Our second system is an incredibly simple and versatile kid carrier, which you get by attaching our all-purpose handle to the sling.It allows you to hold kids more naturally and comfortably, and its slim, breathable design makes it so much easier to use than the other bulky, hot carriers out there. It’s perfect for a wide a range of everyday activities - walking to the park, going to the grocery store, heading to the beach, etc.. And the soft neoprene loop at the bottom of the handle allows kids to walk alongside you (before they inevitably want you to pick them up again).</p>",
